  "The x-chunk commitment binds the committed X BEFORE the challenge but does not prove X equals the served activation: captured rows enter commit_x from the prover's PageStore (host), with no in-kernel GPU commitment during serving, and the plaintext trace_payload_root opening that tied X to the capture in earlier plaintext-trace benchmarks is what this zero-plaintext path replaces (a prover that commits different rows is caught only by other relations, e.g. the relation-4 chain, not by relation 6).",
  "commit_x cost and retained host memory scale linearly with the number of pre-committed chunks (one 2^22-cell ZK-blinded vector, ~96 MiB of host cells, per 64 rows); the blinding draw (os.urandom) dominates per-chunk time.",
  "Only x_attn / x_mlp rows are committed (o_proj / down_proj inputs are not in the schedule); the schedule covers the fresh turn-2 positions only (cached-prefix positions get no draw, as in earlier plaintext-trace benchmarks).",
  "X and Y carry no range proof inside relation 6: |x| <= 2^23 is enforced by the honest prover's partition_rows, not by the circuit; integer faithfulness (sum |W||X| < 2^62) is reported, not proved.",
  "Relation 6 proves Y = W X for the WINDOWED operands (capped exponent window, 23 bits); the window tail vs the exact BF16 / FP8 operands and the served kernel's own FP8 activation quantisation (MoE) are outside the proof; Y is private and is not compared to the served output here.",
  "MoE: the challenged chunk's captured top-8 expert ids (routing metadata, 8 bytes per row) are disclosed to the verifier so it can re-derive the routed-expert tile; they are bound pre-challenge by a salted per-chunk digest in the x_chunks tree, but are not themselves proven to be the router's argmax.",
  "One chunk of n_chunks is drawn uniformly per request: k affected chunks are sampled with probability k / n_chunks (miss probability 1 - k / n_chunks). Turning this sampling rate into end-to-end cheating detection requires additionally binding X to the served GPU capture and Y to the served output (neither is enforced by relation 6 alone).",
  "Single-proof blinding budget per chunk: prove_rel6_zk_bundle enforces at most one proof per committed chunk (identical retries return the cached bundle; distinct challenges raise E_CHUNK_BLINDING_EXHAUSTED); benchmark timing repetitions allocate independently blinded commitments."
 ],
